      "problem": "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={3}^{x}-5{log}_{2}⁡x.$",
      "worked_solution": "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x}-5{log}_{2}⁡x) \\\\  & ={3}^{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & ={3}^{x}\\text{ }\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\frac{5}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
